Network Reliability and Security Remain Important

IP phones depend on reliable network connectivity, appropriate bandwidth and effective quality-of-service configuration. Organizations must also consider device authentication, firmware maintenance, encryption and network segmentation.

Power-over-Ethernet support can simplify deployment by allowing compatible devices to receive power through network cabling. However, the suitability of a particular configuration depends on the installed network and the phone's specifications.

Market Challenges and Competition

The market faces competition from softphones, mobile applications and collaboration platforms that allow employees to make calls without dedicated desk phones. Organizations may choose a combination of physical handsets and software-based communication tools according to job requirements.

Hardware suppliers must therefore compete through call quality, ease of management, reliability, platform compatibility and total cost of ownership.

